        "topic": "Metal extraction methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2012",
        "question_text": "<p>The process of extracting iron from its ore using a blast furnace involves the reduction of <b>iron oxide</b> by which of the following gases?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron oxide ($Fe_2O_3$) is reduced to iron by carbon monoxide ($CO$). The chemical reaction is:<br>$Fe_2O_3 + 3CO \\rightarrow 2Fe + 3CO_2$. Carbon monoxide acts as the reducing agent.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "66237",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Oxygen ($O_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "36935",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "Carbon monoxide ($CO$)",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "25259",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "Carbon dioxide ($CO_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
